# {{ config.project.name }}

Generated by [`0-mcp init`](https://github.com/ssjunior/0-mcp). REST API,
OpenAPI docs and an MCP server, all wired up to your existing
{{ config.project.backend }} database.

## Quick start

```bash
./run.sh
```

The script creates a `uv` virtual environment on first run, installs
dependencies, copies `.env.example` to `.env` if missing, and starts
the dev server. On subsequent runs it skips the install steps and just
boots the server.

If you don't have `uv` yet:

```bash
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
```

## What you get at `http://localhost:8000`

- `/` — index of available endpoints.
- `/docs` — interactive REST docs (Scalar UI).
- `/openapi.json` — OpenAPI 3.1 spec, ready for codegen.
- `/mcp/tools` — agent-facing tool registry, browseable.
- `/mcp/tools.json` — same registry as JSON.
- `/mcp` — JSON-RPC 2.0 endpoint (POST). Agents call tools through here.

## Try it

Start the dev server:

```bash
python manage.py runserver
```

